  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A conversation corner is available, and table discussion remains welcome as long as nearby players can hear their own games.\", \"decision\": \"How should conversation volume be kept comfortable?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe host makes brief rounds and quietly asks tables to lower their voices when neighboring players struggle to hear. A neutral person responds to actual conditions without requiring affected players to begin an awkward exchange.\nEach table chooses a member to notice rising volume and suggest moving extended social conversations to the conversation corner. A familiar participant can offer timely reminders before nearby games are repeatedly interrupted.\nGuests use a small table signal to request quieter discussion, and nearby tables acknowledge it by adjusting their volume. The people affected can communicate their needs directly without having to speak over the conversation themselves."
    }
  ],
